## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates practical knowledge of decoupled processing patterns, per-tenant isolation strategies, feature flag management, and secure configuration handling in Azure. It also assesses the candidate's ability to design a robust end-to-end workflow with appropriate rollback mechanisms.

## Key Concepts

- HTTP-triggered Azure Functions for API endpoints
- Azure Storage Queues for per-tenant message decoupling
- Cosmos DB partitioning using tenantId for data isolation
- Azure App Configuration for feature flags
- Azure Key Vault for secrets management
- CI/CD pipelines across dev, stage, and production environments
- Rollback strategies and poison message handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Function A: HTTP trigger - enqueue to per-tenant queue
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const { tenantId, payload } = req.body;

  if (!tenantId || !payload) {
    context.res = { status: 400, body: 'Missing tenantId or payload' };
    return;
  }

  const queueName = `tenant-${tenantId}-queue`;
  const queueClient = new QueueClient(connectionString, queueName);

  await queueClient.sendMessage(JSON.stringify({ tenantId, payload, timestamp: new Date() }));

  context.res = { status: 202, body: 'Message enqueued' };
};

// Function B: Queue trigger - write to Cosmos DB
module.exports = async function (context, msg) {
  const { tenantId, payload } = JSON.parse(msg.messageText);

  const featureFlags = await getFeatureFlag(`feature-flag-${tenantId}`);
  if (!featureFlags.writeEnabled) {
    context.log(`Writes disabled for tenant: ${tenantId}`);
    return;
  }

  const container = cosmosClient.database('tenant-db').container('events');
  await container.items.create({ id: context.invocationId, tenantId, payload });
};
```

